  <notes>
    <note>Generated once from the sheet, the 2020 counters and the package; edit by hand from here on.</note>
    <note>The counter backs name a set-up area or a city, not hexes, and no input document carries the
      hexes of the areas. The start line is derived: each land hex takes the side of its nearest anchor city
      (Axis: Berlin, Posen, Breslau, Warsaw, Koenigsberg, Bucharest, Ploesti, Helsinki; Russian: Riga, Kaunas,
      Brest, Lvov, Minsk, Tallinn, Leningrad, Kiev, Odessa, Vitebsk, Moscow), and each area's units are
      stacked legally on their own side's hexes nearest that front and nearest the area's anchor. Cities,
      oil fields, junctions and rail links wholly inside a side's hexes start under that side.</note>
    <note>Units with a blank back carry no arrival turn and are not in this scenario; the Special Rail
      army waits in the Off-Map Units Box; the three Stukas are in their box. Riga, Helsinki and
      Sevastopol stand on hexes the sheet classifies as sea, so their units start on the nearest land hex.</note>
  </notes>
